# Home Assistant safety

## Gate

Load on every authorized Home Assistant turn (inventory or mutate). Skip when
the turn never touches Home Assistant.

## Read-only default

These are fine without an extra destructive verb when HA is authorized:

- `GET /api/`, `GET /api/config`
- `GET /api/states`, `GET /api/states/<entity_id>`
- `GET /api/services`
- Area/device registry list reads
- Automation/script inventory reads

Do **not** call services or delete automations unless the user gave an
explicit verb **this turn** naming the entity or object.

## Mutate gates (explicit verb required)

| Risk | Needs this turn |
| --- | --- |
| Turn on/off / toggle | **on**/**off**/**toggle** + entity_id |
| Climate setpoint | **set** + entity_id + temperature |
| Unlock / open cover / garage | **unlock**/**open** + entity_id |
| Disarm alarm | **disarm** + entity_id |
| Delete automation/script/helper | **delete** + object name |
| Restart / reload all YAML | **restart**/**reload** + scope |

Ambiguous "turn everything off" → ask for entity_ids or area; do not
bulk-act across unrelated domains.

## High-risk surfaces

Unlock doors, disarm alarms, open garage covers, and large HVAC changes can
affect physical safety and security. Restate entity_id + effect before the
service call. Prefer skill `home-assistant-service-call` for the checklist.

## Refuse

- Pasting long-lived access tokens or webhook secrets into chat
- Inventing entity_ids
- Absorbing non-HA IoT clouds into this surface
- Restarting Home Assistant when a single service call suffices

## Receipt examples (safe)

Inventory turn: `light.kitchen` friendly Kitchen state `on` — no mutate.

Service turn (authorized): called `light.turn_off` on `light.kitchen`;
follow-up state `off` — no token.

